# Variable Naming: camelCase

All project variables must use **camelCase**.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD
const user_name = "Kim";
const UserAge = 20;
const user-id = 1;

// ✅ GOOD
const userName = "Kim";
const userAge = 20;
const userId = 1;
```

- Local variables, parameters, and object keys you define: `camelCase`
- Do not introduce `snake_case` or `PascalCase` for ordinary variables
- React components and classes still use `PascalCase` (this rule is for variables, not types/components)
